
"""


Linear Regression is used when you want to predict a numerical 
value and you believe the relationship between your input features 
and the target can be approximated by a straight line (or, for 
multiple features, a linear combination).

Real-world applications of Linear Regression

House Price Prediction --> 
Predict the price of a house based on its size.
X: House size → Y: House price


Student Performance Prediction-->
Estimate marks based on study hours.
X: Study hours → Y: Exam marks

Sales Prediction-->
Estimate sales based on advertising expenditure.
X: Advertising budget → Y: Sales revenue


Temperature Analysis--> 
Estimate temperature based on time or other relevant variables.
X: Time → Y: Temperature

Car Price Prediction--> 
Predict a car's resale value using age, mileage, etc.
X: Car features → Y: Resale price

Energy Consumption Prediction--> 
Estimate energy usage based on temperature, time, or building characteristics.
X: Temperature → Y: Energy usage


"""
